                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Pros[/h1]\n• Very fun arcade style bowling game\n• Fun to try for good spots on leaderboards, even though not many people play.\n• Comes with new spiffy unlockable balls based on in-game challenges.\n• Nothing is clunky with the bowling mechanics, everything feels like it should.\n\n\n[h1]Cons[/h1]\n• Sometimes walking over to grab a new ball gets kind of repetitive, [u]ESPECIALLY[/u] in the time trial mode. If there was an option in the menu to be able to vaccuum the ball up into your hand it would make the quality of life much much better.\n\n• In the time trial gamemode, if you completely miss the lane you won't be given a new ball and you will have to teleport to grab it. Seems like an oversight to me.\n\n• Does not come with any sort of level editor, would be a spectacular addition that would greatly increase the longevity of the game in my eyes.\n\n• The menu feels very odd that it would be centered in the middle of the screen, It would look a lot more sleek if the menu came up above your controller that you would then be navigated via the control pad buttons. Not sure how this would interact with the oculus though.\n\n[h1]Main Feature Reccomendations[/h1]\n\n• Add more balls with challenging requirements.\n• Try to implement a level designer with workshop support.\n• Add a normal bowling gamemode.  -  [u]✔ [ADDED][/u]\n• Maybe better implementation of the bowling in the dark in the settings menu. [u]✔ [ADDED][/u]\n• Be able to grab a ball that is not in play from any distance.\n\n\n\nOverall, the idea to make a fun mini-golf type bowling game helped to create a fun casual experience that was implemented fairly well.\n\nFor the price it is a must buy!",
